mod:binding_chain_store;
// 2026-11-11 (landing 177d2b5, row 1: (B) and (b)). THE STORE'S WALK READS A `for` BINDING'S AND A BY-VALUE PARAMETER'S CHAIN AS A LOCAL'S, so a pointer stored
// through one is recorded where a local's is and the growth after it is refused (BORROW-015). One cell a face, its names suffixed with the cell's: each is
// accepted by main (169d6d4) and reads freed memory there (236 at -O0 and -O2, 97 under the detector). Each face's right control is in `binding_chain_store_ok.npk`.
// DEF-587, whole (19 faces, then its face `fv_hq_f2`): `p4`, `p2`, `cb_V`, `cpb_V`, `el_V`, `elc_V`, `elw_V`, `elx_V`, `ff_V`, `ffc_V`, `gV_el_d`, `gV_el_idp`, `gV_el_ter`, `gV_fld_d`, `gV_fld_idp`, `gV_fld_ter`, `gV_loc_d`, `gV_loc_idp`, `gV_loc_ter`, `fv_hq_f2`.
// DEF-604 (10 of its 14 faces; `c_F_swap`, `swb_F`, `x_F_cpq`, `fn1` stay open): `fb11`, `c_F_setq`, `c_F_setqt`, `cb_F`, `cbt_F`, `cpb_F`, `elc_F`, `s_F_d`, `fp1`, `kq2o`. (2026-11-12, landing 177d2b5's row 2, by management_38's ruling "Addendum to row 2's item 1" of Thu 11-12 01:38 EST, item 3: `fn1` closes at row 2, in `for_binding_chain_seed.npk`; `c_F_swap`, `swb_F` and `x_F_cpq` stay open.)
// DEF-647's (B) FACE, A CLASS MADE BY THIS ROW (2026-11-11; management_37's rulings "Addendum 3" of 23:18 and "Addendum 4" of 23:38, in
// briefs/177d-held-rulings-2026-11-02.md): a write through one pointer member of a by-value parameter (a store, a callee or a pointer-receiver method), made while
// a view into a `List` reached through another pointer stored in the parameter is held, is read as a write of that pointer's pointee. The 24 cells below are
// RIGHT programs, refused: the twelve `xq_*_P_ok` (the write is a store; `xq_n2_ok_P_ok` is `fv_hq_ok`'s body) and the twelve `xd_*_met_ok_P_ok` (the write is a
// pointer-receiver method's, `(<-(b.q)).setl(hq)`). Main (169d6d4) accepts each and it runs 67; the misreading is main's own (DEF-647), and (B) gives it something to
// conflict with. Each one's twin with a LOCAL in the parameter's place (`*_L_ok`) is accepted on every build and is in the `_ok` file. They fail closed (LOW) and
// are accepted again when DEF-647's direction lands, after DEF-610 and DEF-348.
error:E5;
struct:K_p4 = { int64:k; };
struct:H_p4 = { List<int64>:l; int64:k; K_p4:kk; };
func:mk_p4 = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(1i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); pass l; };
func:mkh_p4 = H_p4() never fails { pass H_p4{ l: raw mk_p4(), k: 2i64, kk: K_p4{ k: 3i64 } }; };
func:growh_p4 = int64(H_p4->:w) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(@w.l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:growl_p4 = int64(List<int64>->:l) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:fp_p4 = int64->(H_p4->:q) never fails { pass @((<-q).l[0i64]); };
func:idh_p4 = H_p4->(H_p4->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:getl_p4 = List<int64>->(H_p4->:w) never fails { pass @w.l; };
